## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests advanced dynamic programming techniques involving multiple non-overlapping segments with per-element costs—a pattern frequently appearing in interviews for algorithm-intensive roles.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with fixed number of blocks requiring optimal segmentation
- Prefix sum transformations to simplify recurrence relations
- Time-space optimization strategies and solution reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValue(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) P[i+1] = P[i] + A[i];

  const B = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let x = 0; x <= n; x++) B[x] = P[x] - c * x;

  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) dp[i][0] = 0;

  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i][t-1];
      for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        const candidate = dp[j][t-1] + B[i] - B[j];
        if (candidate > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = candidate;
          parent[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let curr = n, currT = k;
  while (currT > 0 && parent[curr][currT] !== -1) {
    const start = parent[curr][currT];
    blocks.unshift([start, curr-1]);
    curr = start;
    currT--;
  }

  return { maxValue: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Implementation Details
- The transformation B[x] = P[x] - c*x captures the net value after maintenance costs
- The nested loop structure ensures we consider all possible segment boundaries
- Parent array enables O(k) reconstruction of optimal segment endpoints

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP with a 3D state on a grid path, a natural but less common extension of standard grid DP.

## Key Concepts

- 3D DP on a grid, path constraints (only right/down), exact boosts
- Bottom-up iteration, reconstruction pointers, space/time considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxBoostOnGrid(grid, k) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array.from({ length: m }, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG)));
  dp[0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        if (i === 0 && j === 0) continue;
        const fromTop = i > 0 ? dp[i-1][j][t] : NEG;
        const fromLeft = j > 0 ? dp[i][j-1][t] : NEG;
        let best = Math.max(fromTop, fromLeft);
        if (best > NEG/2) dp[i][j][t] = best + grid[i][j];
        if (t > 0) {
          const hotTop = i > 0 ? dp[i-1][j][t-1] : NEG;
          const hotLeft = j > 0 ? dp[i][j-1][t-1] : NEG;
          const bestPrev = Math.max(hotTop, hotLeft);
          if (bestPrev > NEG/2) {
            dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], bestPrev + 2*grid[i][j]);
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n-1][m-1][k];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you optimize space if k is large but grid values are small?
- How would you reconstruct the boosted cell coordinates?

## Why This Is Asked
This introduces selecting non-covering, fixed-cost segments, a natural DP with a running max optimization. It tests understanding of prefix sums, state pruning, and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums to compute segment sums in O(1)
- DP over i and t with exactly t segments
- Running maximum best[t] to avoid O(n) inner loop
- Path reconstruction to recover endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueSegments(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length;
  const S = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) S[i]=S[i-1]+A[i-1];
  const negInf = -1e18;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(negInf));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill([-1,-1]));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++) par[0][t]=[-1,-1];
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    let best = negInf; // max of dp[m][t-1]-S[m]
    for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
      best = Math.max(best, dp[i-1][t-1]-S[i-1]);
      const val = best + S[i] - c;
      if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; par[i][t]=[i-1,-1]; }
      if(dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t]; par[i][t]=[i-1,t]; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction (simple version)
  let i=n, t=k, ends=[];
  while(t>0){
    const [pi, pt] = par[i][t] || [-1,-1];
    if(pi===-1) break;
    // approximate end at i, start at some m where dp[m][t-1]-S[m] was max
    // for brevity here, return only values; full reconstruction can be added as needed
    ends.push(i);
    i = pi; t--;
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], ends: ends.reverse() };
}
```

